    {
      "id": "calculate-mid-phase-type",
      "name": "CalculateMidPhaseType",
      "category": "ParticlePairMidPhase",
      "signature": "CalculateMidPhaseType(In Particle 0, In Particle 1)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "In Particle 0",
          "type": "FGeometryParticleHandle*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Particle 1",
          "type": "FGeometryParticleHandle*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "public : EParticlePairMidPhaseType",
      "docs": "@brief Produce collisions for a particle pair\nA FParticlePairMidPhase object is created for every particle pair whose bounds overlap. It is\nresponsible for building a set of potentially colliding shape pairs and running collision\ndetection on those pairs each tick.\n@note The lifetime of midphase objects is handled entirely by the CollisionConstraintAllocator.\nNothing outside of the CollisionConstraintAllocator should hold a pointer to the detector\nor any constraints it creates for more than the duration of the tick.\n@see FShapePairParticlePairMidPhase, FGenericParticlePairMidPhase"
    },
